# Synapse Agent Protocol (SAP) bridge — mainnet enablement.
#
# Copy the relevant keys into the daemon's environment (Render dashboard
# for a hosted daemon, or your shell for a CLI bring-up). The bridge is
# opt-in and defaults OFF; nothing below fires until COVENANT_SAP_ENABLED
# is truthy and the daemon is pointed at mainnet.
#
# The on-chain SAP program is the same address on mainnet and devnet and
# is already deployed + executable, so COVENANT_SAP_PROGRAM_ID does NOT
# need to be set — the default is correct.

# --- cluster + master switch ---------------------------------------------
COVENANT_SOLANA_CLUSTER=mainnet
COVENANT_SAP_ENABLED=1

# --- RPC -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The default public endpoint (api.mainnet-beta.solana.com) is heavily
# rate-limited and WILL throttle under attestation load. Use a keyed
# provider URL.
COVENANT_SAP_MAINNET_RPC_URL=https://mainnet.helius-rpc.com/?api-key=YOUR_KEY
# (COVENANT_SAP_RPC_URL works as a cluster-agnostic fallback.)

# --- signer (the agent's own wallet/authority) ---------------------------
# Solana CLI keypair JSON (64-byte array). This wallet becomes the agent's
# permanent on-chain identity AND pays registration rent + tx fees. Use a
# DEDICATED keypair, not a shared admin wallet. Fund ~0.1 SOL to cover
# register_agent (~0.041 SOL rent) + the first ledger attest + headroom.
COVENANT_SAP_KEYPAIR=/data/keys/sap-signer-mainnet.json

# --- verifier (cross-party attestation; the Witness Loop) ----------------
# A SEPARATELY-keyed wallet, distinct from the signer above. SAP rejects
# self-attestation on-chain (attester must != agent owner), so this signs
# the create_attestation that vouches for the agent's audit root. It pays
# its own attestation tx + rent — fund ~0.02 SOL.
COVENANT_SAP_VERIFIER_KEYPAIR=/data/keys/sap-verifier-mainnet.json

# --- usage counters (optional; persisted on disk) ------------------------
# Where the worker records RPC usage and the daemon's /sap/stats reads it.
# Defaults to $COVENANT_HOME/sap-rpc-stats.json (or ~/.covenant/...).
COVENANT_SAP_STATS_PATH=/data/sap-rpc-stats.json

# --- tuning (optional) ---------------------------------------------------
# COVENANT_SAP_WORKER_TIMEOUT_SECS=30
# COVENANT_SAP_EXPLORER_URL=https://explorer.oobeprotocol.ai

# =========================================================================
# Go-live runbook (one-time, in order)
# =========================================================================
# 1. Generate the two keypairs:
#      solana-keygen new -o /data/keys/sap-signer-mainnet.json
#      solana-keygen new -o /data/keys/sap-verifier-mainnet.json
# 2. Fund: ~0.1 SOL to the signer, ~0.02 SOL to the verifier.
# 3. Build the worker so `covenant-sap-worker` exists:
#      pnpm --filter @covenant/sap-bridge build
# 4. Sanity check (no network):
#      covenant-sap-worker status
#      -> expect cluster=mainnet, enabled=true, hasSigner=true, hasVerifier=true
# 5. Register the agent (one-time, ~0.041 SOL):
#      echo '<AgentManifest JSON>' | covenant-sap-worker publish-agent
#      -> capture the returned agentPda
# 6. Anchor the first audit root (self-anchored ledger):
#      echo '{"rootHashHex":"<64-hex>","releaseTarget":"...","releaseSubject":"...","releaseScope":"...","recordedAt":<unix>}' \
#        | covenant-sap-worker attest-root
# 7. Cross-party attestation (verifier vouches for the agent + root):
#      echo '{"agentPda":"<agentPda>","rootHashHex":"<64-hex>"}' \
#        | covenant-sap-worker attest-agent
# 8. Point the web /sap page at the live agent (Render dashboard):
#      COVENANT_SAP_AGENT_PDA=<agentPda>
#      COVENANT_SOLANA_CLUSTER=mainnet
#      COVENANT_SAP_RPC_URL=<keyed mainnet RPC>
# 9. Verify on-chain: solana account <agentPda> --url <mainnet>  (owner = SAP program).
